From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: asus-zenbook-a16-snapdragon-x2-elite-linux <30148248+hasanaktas@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a6xx: Clamp the MX dependency vote (7.3.6 backport)

The 7.3.6 stable backport of eab0aff8965e ("drm/msm/a6xx: Fix RPMH
dependency votes", b91648f74186) resolves the GPU corners against the
GPU OPP table. On the Zenbook A16 (Glymur, X2 Elite) the 1.85 GHz corner
needs MX level 456, above the highest MX corner (452), so
a6xx_gmu_rpmh_dep_votes_init() fails with "Mx Level 456 not found in the
RPMh list" and leaves the GPU perf table incomplete. Rendering breaks
once RPMh and interconnect sync_state drop the boot-time votes; see
docs/gpu-corruption-7.3.6.md and omacom/omarchy#20199.

Clamp to the highest non-zero MX level instead, as mainline 86f80884
("drm/msm/a6xx: Clamp MX dependency vote") does. This is the adaptation
from omacom/omarchy-pkgs#3545 (romanstingler), tested here on 7.3.6-2.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c | 14 ++++++++------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -1822,14 +1822,16 @@
 		}
 
 		if (j == count) {
-			DRM_DEV_ERROR(dev,
-				      "Mx Level %u not found in the RPMh list\n",
-				      level);
-			DRM_DEV_ERROR(dev, "Available levels:\n");
+			/*
+			 * The GPU arc level can exceed the highest available MX
+			 * corner (e.g. the 1.85 GHz bin on X2-90). Clamp to the
+			 * highest non-zero MX vote instead of failing.
+			 * Upstream: 86f80884 ("drm/msm/a6xx: Clamp MX dependency vote")
+			 */
+			index = 0;
 			for (j = 0; j < count; j++)
-				DRM_DEV_ERROR(dev, "  %u\n", mx[j]);
-
-			return -EINVAL;
+				if (mx[j])
+					index = j;
 		}
 
 		/* Construct the vote */
-- 
